<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  M1K3iOS.entitlements — the iPhone/iPad target's entitlements.

  iOS needs none of the Mac's set: the sandbox is implicit, files arrive through
  the document picker, networking has no entitlement (local-network + Bonjour are
  Info.plist usage keys), and the mic/calendar/location are usage strings + TCC.

  The entries: Increased Memory Limit (iOS jetsams a foreground app at a
  FRACTION of physical RAM; the mobile MLX ceiling only engages back-pressure
  before the kernel's limit if that limit sits above it), Declared Age Range
  (Content Controls' "Set up"), and Private Cloud Compute (PCC, the same
  entitlement the Mac App Store lane carries — Apple's server model).

  The PCC entitlement is an App ID capability: the profile must carry it too.
  Kev enables it in the Apple Developer portal (Identifiers ▸ app.m1k3 ▸
  Additional Capabilities ▸ Private Cloud Compute ▸ tick ▸ Save), then Xcode's
  automatic signing picks it up on the next archive. Without the portal
  capability the entitlement is harmless (PrivateCloudBackends.live() returns nil).

  Signed: Kev + claude-fable-5.1, 2026-09-02, Confidence 0.8 (the entitlement is
  Apple's documented lever for exactly this; the 4 GB ceiling vs the real per-device
  jetsam budget is still the verify-owed measurement — os_proc_available_memory()
  on hardware). Prior: none (new file).
  Review: Kev + claude-opus-5-5, 2026-10-01 — Declared Age Range joins it: Content
  Controls' "Set up" needs the entitlement or the API refuses before any sheet (the
  Mac's tap did nothing in build 375). An App ID capability, so the profile carries
  it. check_store_targets.py pins it. Confidence 0.8 (the Xcode Cloud profile picking
  the capability up is verify-by-archive).
  Review: Kev + claude-opus-4-6, 2026-10-12 — Private Cloud Compute entitlement added:
  PrivateCloudComputeLanguageModel is in the iOS 27 SDK. The backend code
  (PrivateCloudComputeBackend) is @available(iOS 27, *); the shell wires it the same way
  the Mac does (PrivateCloudBackends.live()). Portal capability is Kev's to enable.
  Confidence 0.75 (verify-by-archive + live PCC generation on the phone).
-->
<dict>
	<key>com.apple.developer.kernel.increased-memory-limit</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.developer.declared-age-range</key>
	<true/>
	<key>com.apple.developer.private-cloud-compute</key>
	<true/>
</dict>
</plist>
